      "char_end": 14335,
      "n_chars": 44,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Representations}\\label{sec:repr}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0028",
      "sha256": "fc1caca9c1842e31e9297528fe2cf3c991303d93cc48bdaa855ead1fdb5eab07",
      "char_start": 14337,
      "char_end": 17492,
      "n_chars": 3155,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We compare five representations on PTB-XL. Table~\\ref{tab:repr} gives the input, dimension and pretraining of "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0029",
      "sha256": "eb0d735c1890fac3a0d7e75f319a3a8e5203e9f108fa7c43de1398485fb5edb5",
      "char_start": 17494,
      "char_end": 18642,
      "n_chars": 1148,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Only the hand-crafted features use a single lead. Raw flattening reproduces the 12-lead representation of the "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0030",
      "sha256": "562ded912a4f15995848c230ea8527ee35f8770891a0d8cd2befaf7cc4d9a3d8",
      "char_start": 18644,
      "char_end": 19196,
      "n_chars": 552,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We chose the two foundation models by three criteria. Both have public weights and take 12-lead input. They di"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0031",
      "sha256": "a927c30fd2147c01074d8d16f5e92f9368bd92d3f0a57f770d581fed8361ef81",
      "char_start": 19198,
      "char_end": 20555,
      "n_chars": 1357,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "On MIT-BIH the rhythm features do not apply to single beats, so three beat representations are compared. The r"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0032",
      "sha256": "31091516a4c2e5d69c3c68af7f70f1dc4c0afc33453bdbd7caa04b7d621e9fea",
      "char_start": 20557,
      "char_end": 22069,
