      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0041",
      "sha256": "9d4976f410cdbad7019b2c94b740986782907e1507211b0674cc09b187abce23",
      "char_start": 31495,
      "char_end": 31539,
      "n_chars": 44,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Federated clustering simulation}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0042",
      "sha256": "1a46f042c73d8e5afb37c9897cb454a3362469e4d9f204184c8a8ce27f8adec3",
      "char_start": 31541,
      "char_end": 32786,
      "n_chars": 1245,
      "section": "Federated clustering simulation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "To probe deployment under data siloing we use federated $k$-means, with centroid aggregation in the manner of "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0043",
      "sha256": "38af922a42eab1675171bc8e32009b028472bf2fc5bbc7d98f5ff5312845354b",
      "char_start": 32788,
      "char_end": 32824,
      "n_chars": 36,
      "section": "Federated clustering simulation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Results}\\label{sec:results}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0044",
      "sha256": "f22d7c5177226ed2a271b44445b924bc3afb403f589104e20cba7d49ecd33056",
      "char_start": 32826,
      "char_end": 32881,
      "n_chars": 55,
      "section": "Results",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Clustering by representation and algorithm}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0045",
      "sha256": "a802dece88961f8d479b11e7625153c9298bc8e7bff9de890fb7a43a88186c0e",
      "char_start": 32883,
      "char_end": 33510,
      "n_chars": 627,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Table~\\ref{tab:main} and Fig.~\\ref{fig:heatmap} summarise the PTB-XL benchmark. ECGFounder clusters best (ARI "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0046",
      "sha256": "18fa13d2f2e8447d4fd2b903f90da51d307d1f464b9fdc8d4492cc6b7fe65d8f",
      "char_start": 33512,
      "char_end": 35323,
      "n_chars": 1811,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0047",
      "sha256": "c81cc6cbd414d183e75305acf6368839770497aab27b704731945d2ffd5e7a97",
      "char_start": 35325,
      "char_end": 35934,
      "n_chars": 609,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0048",
      "sha256": "72f50a3a6e3e045c41960ac9c94378fc36220872d35075cbc58fb47453b06280",
      "char_start": 35936,
      "char_end": 37208,
      "n_chars": 1272,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Across ten seeds the $k$-means solutions are stable. The seed standard deviation of their ARI is 0.000 for raw"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0049",
      "sha256": "8ba7b4beede0677c6c9e620be54e24883d840e184860535cf492f318552a86ac",
      "char_start": 37210,
      "char_end": 38035,
      "n_chars": 825,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The two foundation models do not behave as one category. ECGFounder clusters strongly while HuBERT-ECG does no"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0050",
      "sha256": "ef6f5eb701fcd5b77c748c7598a8adc3cb8a57d402b192a360e8f10fe524facf",
      "char_start": 38037,
      "char_end": 38084,
      "n_chars": 47,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Separability is not clusterability}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0051",
      "sha256": "881662c6b1922a4794763c1f548b5394c35fd2abfaf5594575c61cc4204b75ce",
      "char_start": 38086,
      "char_end": 39422,
      "n_chars": 1336,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The supervised ceilings (last column of Table~\\ref{tab:main}, Fig.~\\ref{fig:sep}) expose the gap between separ"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0052",
      "sha256": "78fc3a080c3fa27d5ca528bba5be7e65386f89f10bd474c0e98fd38555367d81",
      "char_start": 39424,
      "char_end": 40046,
      "n_chars": 622,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Each result has a likely explanation, and the study did not test these mechanisms directly. ECGFounder was pre"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0053",
      "sha256": "5085990acaabcf6e7b60e66e0f6230635319c3a5b505a3400b4bfd122fbc97a8",
      "char_start": 40048,
      "char_end": 40795,
      "n_chars": 747,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "HuBERT-ECG was pretrained by self-supervision without diagnostic labels \\cite{hubertecg2024}, and here it saw "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0054",
      "sha256": "b8a84288b9d8ef1e4608523b57e696bdc01b7d5a6889d70051b52609ed427f23",
      "char_start": 40797,
      "char_end": 41327,
      "n_chars": 530,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Raw flattening and the conv-AE score at chance for different reasons. With $k$-means, raw flattening places on"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0055",
      "sha256": "bac923c30f75259f22873647879f24230069eeaa51751fe57209e267d5e0d6d8",
      "char_start": 41329,
      "char_end": 42243,
      "n_chars": 914,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0056",
      "sha256": "b3eb476ff58189ffd6535514e14b0a4144a30aa0d3d2711f3e346b848b326a4d",
      "char_start": 42245,
      "char_end": 42277,
      "n_chars": 32,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{The silhouette trap}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0057",
      "sha256": "b539a29832e878beb7c1cbd7dd50b9a22b04363793ca1638f4af087ab1aac298",
      "char_start": 42279,
      "char_end": 42916,
      "n_chars": 637,
      "section": "The silhouette trap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Internal indices mislead here in a specific, reproducible way. Raw flattening with Ward attains a silhouette o"
    },
